pageType: content
background:
  type: solid
  color: "$bg"
elements:
  # ---------- header ----------
  - elementId: kicker
    elementType: text
    bounds: [64, 38, 700, 16]
    content:
      style: "$kicker"
      wrap: false
      align: [left, middle]
      text: |
        SOLUTION 2 OF 2 - ONTOLOGY · FIXES THE MEANING
  - elementId: title
    elementType: text
    bounds: [64, 58, 720, 44]
    content:
      style: "$title"
      wrap: false
      align: [left, middle]
      text: |
        What is an ontology?
  - elementId: title-rule
    elementType: shape
    bounds: [64, 118, 832, 1]
    shapeName: rect
    fill: {type: solid, color: "$line"}

  # ---------- left column: definition + bullets ----------
  - elementId: definition
    elementType: text
    bounds: [64, 140, 470, 108]
    content:
      fontSize: 17.5
      color: "$ink"
      lineHeight: 1.5
      align: [left, top]
      text: |
        <p>A <strong>formal model of what exists in the business</strong> and how those things relate - it defines <strong>meaning</strong>, not math.</p>
  - elementId: bullets
    elementType: text
    bounds: [64, 262, 470, 210]
    content:
      fontSize: 12.5
      color: "$ink"
      lineHeight: 1.5
      align: [left, top]
      text: |
        <p><span style="color:$ont">■</span> <strong>The nouns and verbs of the domain.</strong> Parties, contracts, terminals, custody tickets - and the relationships between them, like sold-to, payer, and ship-to as a location.</p>
        <p style="margin-top:11px"><span style="color:$ont">■</span> <strong>Machine-readable meaning.</strong> Written so people and AI can validate, connect, and reason over it - not just read it in a wiki.</p>
        <p style="margin-top:11px"><span style="color:$ont">■</span> <strong>Meaning outlives implementation.</strong> The concept of a customer survives every system migration; today's formulas and tools may not.</p>
        <p style="margin-top:11px"><span style="color:$ont">■</span> <strong>A spectrum, not a two-year project.</strong> Start with a glossary, add hierarchy and relationships, formalize only where the need is real.</p>

  # ---------- right column: concept graph ----------
  - elementId: graph-label
    elementType: text
    bounds: [580, 130, 316, 14]
    content:
      fontSize: 10
      color: "$muted"
      letterSpacing: 1.5
      wrap: false
      align: [left, middle]
      text: |
        WHAT THINGS ARE, AND HOW THEY RELATE
  # party node
  - elementId: party-node
    elementType: shape
    bounds: [580, 205, 92, 48]
    shapeName: rect
    fill: {type: solid, color: "$ont"}
  - elementId: party-node-text
    elementType: text
    bounds: [580, 205, 92, 48]
    content:
      fontSize: 12.5
      color: "$white"
      bold: true
      align: [center, middle]
      text: |
        Party
  # edges party -> roles
  - elementId: edge-soldto
    elementType: line
    bounds: [672, 170, 68, 59]
    viewBox: [68, 59]
    points: "0,59 68,0"
    curve: sharp
    arrow: [null, arrow]
    border: {style: solid, width: 1.2, color: "$ont"}
  - elementId: edge-payer
    elementType: line
    bounds: [672, 229, 68, 2]
    viewBox: [68, 2]
    points: "0,1 68,1"
    curve: sharp
    arrow: [null, arrow]
    border: {style: solid, width: 1.2, color: "$ont"}
  - elementId: edge-label
    elementType: text
    bounds: [656, 196, 90, 12]
    content:
      fontSize: 9
      color: "$muted"
      wrap: false
      align: [center, middle]
      text: |
        plays role of
  # role chips
  - elementId: role-1
    elementType: shape
    bounds: [740, 148, 132, 44]
    shapeName: rect
    fill: {type: solid, color: "$ontSoft"}
    border: {style: solid, width: 1.2, color: "$ont"}
  - elementId: role-1-text
    elementType: text
    bounds: [740, 148, 132, 44]
    content:
      fontSize: 9
      color: "$muted"
      align: [center, middle]
      lineHeight: 1.3
      text: |
        <p><strong><span style="font-size:11.5px; color:$ont">Sold-to</span></strong></p>
        <p>on the contract</p>
  - elementId: role-2
    elementType: shape
    bounds: [740, 208, 132, 44]
    shapeName: rect
    fill: {type: solid, color: "$ontSoft"}
    border: {style: solid, width: 1.2, color: "$ont"}
  - elementId: role-2-text
    elementType: text
    bounds: [740, 208, 132, 44]
    content:
      fontSize: 9
      color: "$muted"
      align: [center, middle]
      lineHeight: 1.3
      text: |
        <p><strong><span style="font-size:11.5px; color:$ont">Payer</span></strong></p>
        <p>who settles the invoice</p>
  - elementId: role-3
    elementType: shape
    bounds: [580, 268, 156, 44]
    shapeName: rect
    fill: {type: solid, color: "$ontSoft"}
    border: {style: solid, width: 1.2, color: "$ont"}
  - elementId: role-3-text
    elementType: text
    bounds: [580, 268, 156, 44]
    content:
      fontSize: 9
      color: "$muted"
      align: [center, middle]
      lineHeight: 1.3
      text: |
        <p><strong><span style="font-size:11.5px; color:$ont">Ship-to / Site</span></strong></p>
        <p>location / terminal, not a party role</p>
  - elementId: graph-caption
    elementType: text
    bounds: [580, 326, 316, 46]
    content:
      fontSize: 10.5
      color: "$muted"
      lineHeight: 1.4
      align: [left, top]
      text: |
        <p>One party, several roles (sold-to, bill-to, payer). In the O2C demo the invoice is billed to the <strong>payer</strong>, not the sold-to. Bill-to is a separate role. The ship-to is a location (a terminal), not a party role. Mixing those is what makes unbilled by customer unreliable.</p>

  # ---------- right column: spectrum ----------
  - elementId: spectrum-label
    elementType: text
    bounds: [580, 384, 316, 14]
    content:
      fontSize: 10
      color: "$muted"
      letterSpacing: 1.5
      wrap: false
      align: [left, middle]
      text: |
        HOW FORMAL DOES IT NEED TO BE?
  - elementId: spectrum-marker-label
    elementType: text
    bounds: [640, 404, 190, 12]
    content:
      fontSize: 9.5
      color: "$ont"
      bold: true
      wrap: false
      align: [center, middle]
      text: |
        Most teams need the middle
  - elementId: spectrum-marker
    elementType: shape
    bounds: [730, 420, 12, 10]
    shapeName: triangle
    fill: {type: solid, color: "$ont"}
  - elementId: spectrum-bar
